  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale up TB and HIV interventions in Tanzania - Tanzania (United Republic) (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania (United Republic), TB/HIVThis program has the following goals: To achieve universal access to comprehensive HIV prevention, treatment, care and support services in order to significantly minimise the transmission of new HIV.  To reduce the incidence by 25% and mortality by 50% of TB and Leprosy by 2020. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: Increased adoption of safer sexual practices (reduced risk behaviours), increased healthier behaviours and increased uptake of comprehensive HIV and AIDS services (prevention, treatment, care and support).  Objective 2: Increased utilization of condoms during high-risk sex among women and men aged between 15-49 years..  Objective 3: 80% of all eligible PLHIVs are put on and retained on appropriate ART regimen by the year 2017.  Objective 4: Increase TB case detection by 30% by 2020 from 2013 levels..  Objective 5: Increase MDR cases detected and enrolled for treatment from 17% of estimated total cases among those notified to 84% by 2020.  Objective 6: Expand TB/HIV collaborative to ensure 100% of all TB patients are tested for HIV and 100% of HIV patients are screened for TB by 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
